      "answer": "$4$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$a(1+r)=15$. B1 — accept $a(1-r^2)/(1-r)=15$. $\\frac{a}{1-r}=\\frac{125}{7}$. B1. $\\frac{125}{7}(1-r)(1+r)=15$. M1 — eliminate $a$. $1-r^2=\\frac{105}{125}$. M1. $r^2=\\frac4{25}$, leading to $r=-\\frac25$. A1 — condone $\\frac25$ or $\\pm\\frac25$. $a=\\frac{125}{7}\\times\\frac75=25$. A1 — ignore second answer. Third term $=25\\times\\frac4{25}=4$. A1 CAO. Alternative method 1: $a(1+r)=15$. B1. $\\frac{a}{1-r}=\\frac{125}{7}$. B1. $7(15-15r)=(125-125r)(1-r^2)$. M1. $125r^3-125r^2-20r+20=0$. M1. $r=-\\frac25$; condone extra answer $r=1$ and condone $\\frac25$ or $\\pm\\frac25$. A1. $a=25$. A1 — ignore second answer. Third term $=4$. A1 CAO. Alternative method 2: $a(1+r)=15$. B1. $\\frac{a}{1-r}=\\frac{125}{7}$. B1. $\\frac{a}{1-(15/a-1)}=\\frac{125}{7}$. M1 — eliminate $r$. $7a^2-250a+1875=0$. M1. $a=25$ or $\\frac{75}{7}$; condone the extra answer $\\frac{75}{7}$. A1. $r=-\\frac25$. A1 — ignore second answer. Third term $=25\\times\\frac4{25}=4$. A1 CAO. Total 7.",
